# Conclusion

## Verdict

```julia; echo = false, results = "tex"
print(acceptance_conclusion_text())
```

## Summary by scenario

Every scenario of this report, the number of comparisons it made against reference values
(*Checks*) and the number of recorded outcomes that failed (*Failures*).

  * For the plasma, urine and pharmacodynamics scenarios a failure is a comparison outside
    the acceptance criteria.
  * `PKG-TEST` makes no numeric comparison: its single recorded outcome is the result of the
    package test suite, so its *Checks* is zero and a failure there means the suite failed.
  * A required scenario whose code chunk errored out produces no rows at all and is listed as
    NOT REPORTED; its results table is then missing from the Results section as well.

The integration method is named in the table by its `calcm` value (`:lint`, `:luld`, `:logt`)
and `dt` stands for the dose time; the Results section above spells each scenario out in full.

```julia; echo = false, results = "tex"
show(latexify(acceptance_summary_table(); latex=false))
```
Table: Comparisons and verdict by scenario

## Divergence journal

Everything that failed acceptance, one row per item: a comparison outside the criteria
stated in section *Acceptance criteria* ($r_{tol}$ = `j ACCEPT_RTOL`, $a_{tol}$ =
`j ACCEPT_ATOL`), a failed test suite run, or a required scenario that did not report. For a
comparison the row carries the computed value, the reference value, their difference and the
relative error $|x - x_{ref}| / |x_{ref}|$.

```julia; echo = false, results = "tex"
print(acceptance_journal_block())
```

```julia; echo = false, results = "tex"
# The Conclusion marks itself once its tables are rendered. A chunk that
# errored out records nothing, so a report that lost its verdict is caught by
# the required-scenario check outside the document generator. The mark is made
# before the journal is written, so that the file written here already carries
# it; `validation.jl` writes the journal again in any case.
acceptance_mark("CONCLUSION", true, "conclusion rendered")
acceptance_write_journal()
print("Full comparison log: docs/src/validation_acceptance.tsv. " *
      "Divergence journal: docs/src/validation_divergences.tsv.")
```

